usage: orion_pro_publish.py [-h] [--local] [--mode {plan,publish}]
                            [--admission ADMISSION]
                            [--admission-sha256 ADMISSION_SHA256]
                            [--dataset-generation DATASET_GENERATION]
                            [--catalog-generation CATALOG_GENERATION]
                            [--editions EDITIONS] [--receipt RECEIPT]

Publish the existing four Pro V1 readers from admitted, retained typed SQL.
This first execution boundary is deliberately an explicit owned-local mode. An
admission document describes synthetic business scope; its digest provides
integrity, never source acceptance or permission to publish real data. Neither
source bodies nor providers are opened. Ready outputs and historical pointers
remain immutable. Dirty rows are durable hints, not a queue to delete or
reset.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --local               Require explicit owned local PostgreSQL; no remote
                        mode exists
  --mode {plan,publish}
  --admission ADMISSION
                        Explicit retained synthetic business admission JSON
  --admission-sha256 ADMISSION_SHA256
  --dataset-generation DATASET_GENERATION
  --catalog-generation CATALOG_GENERATION
  --editions EDITIONS   Comma-separated admitted edition BIGINT IDs
  --receipt RECEIPT
